  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Any general point on the line is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2,</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br />This point most satisfy <math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>21</mn></math><br /><br />Hence <math><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>21</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math><br /><br />So, the point of intersection of line and plane is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>)</mo></math><br /><br />So, equation of plane P = 0 is <math><mn>2</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>37</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><br />Hence, distance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> from origin is<br /><br /><math><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>37</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>37</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>",
